--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture (matches established sibling W7 pages: AlertRulesPage / ActiveSessionsPage)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- MVVM, no business logic in code-behind. The view binds VehicleAccessPageViewModel and
  renders the pure VehicleAccessDisplay projection; all branch selection / formatting /
  i18n happen in the headless Model. State changes are marshalled onto the UI thread via
  DispatcherQueue. The page + view-model are IDisposable (CA1001) and unsubscribe on Unloaded.
- Data port IVehicleAccessFeed (web hooks) -> generated C# OpenAPI client (ADR-004), the
  feed constructed per vehicle so each call fills the vehicleID path slot exactly once:
    useVehicle               -> get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID                                 GET    /vehicles/{vehicleID}/            (display_name → header)
    useVehicleDrivers        -> get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_drivers                         GET    /vehicles/{vehicleID}/drivers
    useVehicleInvitations    -> get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_invitations                     GET    /vehicles/{vehicleID}/invitations
    useRefreshVehicleDrivers -> post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_drivers_refresh                POST   /vehicles/{vehicleID}/drivers/refresh
    useRefreshVehicleInvit.. -> post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_invitations_refresh            POST   /vehicles/{vehicleID}/invitations/refresh
    useRemoveVehicleDriver   -> delete_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_drivers                      DELETE /vehicles/{vehicleID}/drivers      { share_user_id }
    useCreateVehicleInvit..  -> post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_invitations                    POST   /vehicles/{vehicleID}/invitations
    useRevokeVehicleInvit..  -> post_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_invitations_invitationID_revoke POST  /vehicles/{vehicleID}/invitations/{invitationID}/revoke
  (op ids cross-checked against apps/windows/Generated ApiEndpoints.All — all 8 present;
   asserted by the 8 ClientFeed_* request-shaping tests.)
- Shared Fluent components reused (no web pixel-cloning, ADR-005/006):
    TsGlassPanel (the two panels), PageTitle / Subhead / Caption (header), SectionTitle
    (panel headings), Label (column headers), Text / TextBlock (cells), TsBadge (row count +
    role chip), TsButton (refresh / invite / remove / revoke), TsCopyButton (invite link),
    TsStatusBadge (invitation status dot+word), TsDateTime (expiry), TsSkeleton (loading),
    TsErrorDisplay (error+retry), TsEmptyState (empty), TsConfirmDialog (remove + revoke).
    All colours/typography come from the W1 design tokens (Tokens.xaml) via DisplayTokens /
    StatusResources — no hardcoded hex, no ad-hoc typography.
- i18n: every visible literal flows through ILocalizer.GetString("<key>","<English fallback>").
  The 27 manifest keys already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw and resolve
  through the WinUI resource bridge (Localization.Get); headless tests assert every key is
  requested (RecordingLocalizer) and that the English fallbacks match the web copy verbatim.
- Units: this page has no SI-unit fields (driver/invitation metadata); nothing stored/computed
  non-SI. The lone timestamp (expires_at) renders through the shared TsDateTime boundary.
- Live data: this page has no live/SSE source (the web page is two TanStack queries only), so
  no >2min staleness chrome is applicable (matches the web source).
- Null safety: tolerant JSON parsers (VehicleDriver/VehicleInvitation.ParseList) never throw on
  partial rows; every optional field em-dashes at the display boundary; the remove / copy /
  revoke affordances are gated exactly as the web (share_user_id != null / invite_url / status
  === 'pending'). An empty vehicle id disables both queries (web enabled: !!vehicleId).

