Pre-existing build blocker unblocked (required to compile the shared TeslaSync.App assembly)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The branch HEAD did not build (BUILD_EXIT=1) before this change due to two pre-existing
CA1822 analyzer-as-error violations in a SIBLING page, unrelated to vehicle-access:
    feature-views/MQTTInspectorPage/MQTTInspectorPage.cs(329): BuildConnectionContent
    feature-views/MQTTInspectorPage/MQTTInspectorPage.cs(389): BuildThroughputContent
Both members do not touch instance data; the analyzer's own prescribed fix (mark `static`)
was applied verbatim (zero behaviour change — both are pure builders over their `display`
param + the `const ChartHeight`). VehicleAccessPage compiles into the same TeslaSync.App
assembly, so this was the minimal change needed to make `dotnet build TeslaSync.sln` green and
verify the new page. No other MQTTInspectorPage logic was touched.

